      diet: "Labs are one of the most obesity-prone breeds, and part of that is genetic. A 14 base pair deletion in the POMC gene runs at a 12 percent allele frequency, with about 22 percent of Labradors carrying at least one copy, and each copy adds a mean 1.90 kg of body weight and about half a body condition point along with greater food motivation. That is an effect measured feeding and daily exercise can absorb, not a sentence, and most overweight Labs are overweight for ordinary reasons. Measure food rather than eyeballing it, keep treats to about 10 percent of daily calories, and aim for a lean body condition where the ribs are easily felt but not seen. It matters: Labradors carry 2.83 times the odds of osteoarthritis and 1.62 times the odds of obesity compared with other dogs, and musculoskeletal disorders are the leading cause of death in the breed at 24.5 percent.",
      enrichment: "Bred to retrieve all day in the field, Labs need sustained aerobic exercise: swimming, fetch, running, or hiking. They also need training and mental challenges. Without adequate exercise and stimulation, Labs become destructive chewers and boisterous inside the home. They are among the easiest dogs to train due to their food drive and eagerness to please.",
